    "Immediate management post-carotid artery stenting (CAS) involves monitoring the access site and neurological and hemodynamic function. Clopidogrel and aspirin are recommended for antiplatelet therapy. Patients should cease smoking and manage conditions like hypertension, hyperlipidemia, and diabetes. Anticoagulation can be achieved with unfractionated heparin, and several pharmacological agents may treat hemodynamic derangements. Postoperative care includes serial follow-ups with imaging to monitor restenosis. The CaRESS trial assessed nonrandomized comparisons of carotid endarterectomy and CAS in patients.": []
